{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "growth_sectional_lr2m_mms",
    "description": "MMS driver for the two condensational-growth rules of grids/sectional_volume_1d (growth_lr2m_D_bin_closed for section NUMBER, growth_lr2m_tracer_D_bin_closed for a volume-carried quantity): the sectional moments of the continuous growth equation dn/dt + d(G n)/dv = 0 with the volume-proportional growth law G(v) = lam v. Two spatial cells (NCELL = 2, bound at the import edges) carry the two growth directions: cell 1 GROWS (lam = +lam0) and cell 2 SHRINKS (lam = -lam0), i.e. lam = sigma lam0 with sigma = 3 - 2 cell, so both upwind branches of the edge flux (sectional_lr2m_number_flux_up / _down and their tracer forms) are exercised in one run. The size grid is the grid's shared geometric test grid mms_sections_vb (grids/sectional_volume_1d/mesh/mms_sections.esm): NBIN sections spanning one doubling of particle volume, vb[kn] = 2^((kn-1)/NBIN). EXACT SOLUTION. Along characteristics v = v0 e^{sigma lam0 t}, so n(v,t) = e^{-sigma lam0 t} n0(v e^{-sigma lam0 t}) with the compactly supported C2 bump n0(u) = 64 s^3 (1-s)^3, s = clamp((u - c)/w, 0, 1), w = 0.3, c = 0.9 + 0.3 cell (cell 1 on [1.2, 1.5], cell 2 on [1.5, 1.8]). At t = 0.2 the supports are [1.466, 1.832] and [1.228, 1.474]: inside [1, 2], so up to t = 0.2 the exact solution never reaches either end of the size range and the rules' CLOSED ends (zero flux through vb[1] and vb[NBIN+1]) are exact for it. The section moments of the exact solution are closed form (derivation in grids/sectional_volume_1d/mesh/mms_bump.esm); the ic equations apply its CLOSED templates mms_bump_number / mms_bump_volume, which read only their parameters and NBIN and so may be applied in that build-time position (unlike the vb observed, which they never read). The esm-spec 6.6.5 test references spell the same moments inline, in the same Horner form: the inline-test oracle evaluates a reference without resolving template references (verified in the Julia binding at EarthSciAST 84ed0627e), so a reference may not apply a template at all (AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat). The t = 0 assertions therefore also cross-check the templated ic against the independent inline spelling. MODEL. The tracer m (NTRACER = 1) is the section dry VOLUME itself, and the volume moment the number rule reads is V = m[:, :, 1]: the shape in which a sectional aerosol model carries its component volumes. Number obeys dN/dt = -D(lam*N, V, wrt: bin) (transfer only: growth does not change number), and the volume-carried quantity dm/dt = lam m - D(lam*m, N, V, wrt: bin): the in-section growth lam m = int G n dv plus the transfer of the grown volume between sections. WHAT IS MEASURED. (1) Relative L2 errors of N at t = 0.2 and of m at t = 0.1 over every (cell, section): the two convergence cases (tests/conformance/convergence/growth_sectional_lr2m_mms and growth_sectional_lr2m_tracer_mms) each take the FIRST L2_error assertion at their assert_time, so the number and tracer measurements sit at different times to be selectable. The reconstruction is linear within a section and fixed by its two moments, so it is exact for a locally linear density, and the upwind edge value then carries an O(h^2) error: the rules are second order (order:2) on smooth data. Where the bump is well resolved the section means sit in the middle third and the full linear profile is used; in the sections at the edges of the support (where n0 and its first two derivatives vanish) the triangle cut-backs and the 1 % edge band act as a limiter. Their share of the error falls with resolution, so the observed order is near 1.3 at NBIN = 16..32 and settles near 2 from NBIN = 32; the convergence cases therefore sweep NBIN = 32..256. (2) Conservation of number, the per-cell total Ntot = sectional_total(N) (grids/sectional_volume_1d/grid.esm): at t = 0.2 with the bump inside the size range (interior telescoping), and at t = 1 (test closed_ends_conserve_number), by which time both bumps have left [1, 2] -- cell 1's support is [3.26, 4.08] and cell 2's [0.55, 0.66] -- so every particle has piled up against the closed top or bottom end and only exact zero-flux ends keep Ntot at its initial value.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:sectional_volume_1d",
      "equation:condensational_growth",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Gelbard, F., Tambour, Y., & Seinfeld, J. H. (1980). Sectional representations for simulating aerosol dynamics. Journal of Colloid and Interface Science, 76(2), 541-556.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9797(80)90394-X"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Growth": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/sectional_volume_1d/rules/growth_lr2m_D_bin_closed.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NCELL": 2,
            "NTRACER": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/sectional_volume_1d/rules/growth_lr2m_tracer_D_bin_closed.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NCELL": 2,
            "NTRACER": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/sectional_volume_1d/grid.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NCELL": 2,
            "NTRACER": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/sectional_volume_1d/mesh/mms_sections.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NCELL": 2,
            "NTRACER": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/sectional_volume_1d/mesh/mms_bump.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NCELL": 2,
            "NTRACER": 1
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "N": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "cell",
            "bin"
          ],
          "description": "Section number moment, N[c,j] = integral of n dv over section j of cell c."
        },
        "m": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "um^3/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "cell",
            "bin",
            "tracer"
          ],
          "description": "Volume-carried quantity per section (NTRACER = 1): the section dry volume, m[c,j,1] = integral of v n dv over section j."
        },
        "V": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "um^3/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "cell",
            "bin"
          ],
          "description": "Section volume moment the reconstruction reads, V[c,j] = m[c,j,1]."
        },
        "lam": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "cell",
            "bin"
          ],
          "description": "Relative volume growth rate of each section, lam[c,j] = sigma lam0 with sigma = 3 - 2 c: +lam0 (growth) in cell 1, -lam0 (shrinkage) in cell 2, uniform over the sections."
        },
        "grow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "um^3/m^3/s",
          "shape": [
            "cell",
            "bin",
            "tracer"
          ],
          "description": "In-section growth of the volume-carried quantity, lam m = integral of G n dv over the section with G = lam v."
        },
        "Ntot": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "cell"
          ],
          "description": "Total number of each cell over all sections, sectional_total(N): conserved exactly by the closed, telescoping number rule."
        },
        "lam0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Magnitude of the relative growth rate. The exact solution in the ic and references (mms_bump.esm) is spelled for lam0 = 1."
        },
        "vb": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "um^3",
          "shape": [
            "bin_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Section edge volumes, the grid's shared geometric test grid mms_sections_vb (vb[kn] = 2^((kn-1)/NBIN)); read by the rules by bare name."
        }
      },
