      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_sectional_growth_both_directions",
          "description": "Sectional moments of the exact solution n = e^{-sigma t} n0(v e^{-sigma t}) (cell 1 growing, cell 2 shrinking, lam0 = 1) on the geometric test grid. The t = 0 assertions pin the ic wiring; the later L2_error assertions bound the relative errors of N at t = 0.2 and of the volume-carried m at t = 0.1 (distinct times, so that each convergence case selects its own quantity) at the default NBIN = 8 (per-resolution values pinned in the golden/errors.json of tests/conformance/convergence/growth_sectional_lr2m_mms and growth_sectional_lr2m_tracer_mms). The Ntot assertions require each cell's total number at t = 0.2 to equal its exact initial value 19.2/140 (mms_bump.esm) to round-off.",
